Subject: [PATCH] Keep the legacy provision policy alias and make provision_policy writable

The custom entitlement exposed two Terraform attributes for one API field: the
create-only provision_policy projection and the entity's computed
provisioner_policy. The update serializer built the request from the server-read
mirror, so a configured policy never reached the API, and every node of the
create-only subtree carried a replacement modifier, so a newly configured policy
planned a destroy/recreate.

This keeps the public surface intact. The entity's computed provisioner_policy
stays exactly where it was - same path, same nested types and flags - and is
marked deprecated as a read-only mirror of the same server policy.
provision_policy becomes the sole configured write source: its replacement
modifiers are removed, the replacement wording is dropped from its descriptions,
and the update request is built from the configured value, serialized under the
entity's wire name provisionerPolicy. Create is unchanged.

Co-authored-by: c1-squire-dev[bot] <c1-squire-dev[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>

